{"qid":"Q781","names":["Antigua and Barbuda"],"title":"Antigua and Barbuda","endonym":{"native":"Antigua and Barbuda","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Antigua and Barbuda achieved full independence on 1 November 1981, with Vere Cornwall Bird of the Antigua Labour Party as its first prime minister, after having held associated-state status within the British sphere since 1967. The country is a constitutional monarchy within the Commonwealth, with Charles III as head of state represented by a governor-general. Its economy depends heavily on tourism centred on Antigua's beaches and English Harbour, site of the restored eighteenth-century British naval dockyard; since 2014 Prime Minister Gaston Browne has led the government following successive Labour victories.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Antigua and Barbuda's territory—the islands of Antigua (280 km²), Barbuda (161 km²), and the islet of Redonda—is precisely defined and uncontested.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Antigua and Barbuda","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antigua_and_Barbuda"},{"label":"Britannica: Antigua and Barbuda","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Antigua-and-Barbuda"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Vere Cornwall Bird","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vere_Cornwall_Bird"}],"britannica":"place/Antigua-and-Barbuda","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Antigua and Barbuda","rulers":[{"qid":"Q9682","name":"Elizabeth II","start":1981,"end":2022,"image":"Queen Elizabeth II official portrait for 1959 tour (retouched) (cropped) (3-to-4 aspect ratio).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Queen%20Elizabeth%20II%